{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"agent_message","text":"The baseline will use one fused recurrent Triton kernel: each lane owns one `(batch, channel)` state across the full sequence, so it removes thousands of framework launches and writes only the required outputs. I’m preserving each stabilization step explicitly and using the device’s accurate exponential routine because the tolerance is near single-precision roundoff."}}
